= Citation — Simple =

A citation is an explicit reference from one scholarly work or research object to another source, contribution, dataset, software artifact, or prior work.

Citations provide attribution, provenance, context, evidence trails, and machine-readable relationships within the scholarly record. They can indicate use, comparison, criticism, background, or disagreement.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* citation ≠ endorsement
* citation count ≠ quality

